-- title:
--   Nonsplit tori and their normalizers in PSL₂ over a finite field
-- statement:
--   Let F be a finite field of cardinality p^f, where p is prime, and put d=gcd(|F|-1,2). There is a cyclic nonsplit torus S in PSL₂(F) of order (|F|+1)/d with normalizer of order 2|S|. Its normalizer is generated by S and an involution w outside S which acts on S by inversion. Every nontrivial subgroup of S has this same normalizer. Moreover, if a nonidentity element of S is conjugated back into S, the conjugating element belongs to the normalizer. Finally, the projective image of any determinant-one 2-by-2 matrix whose squared trace is not 4 and which has no eigenvector over F belongs to a conjugate of S.
--
--   This is the explicit nonsplit-torus package in the original CFSG formalization of Huppert II.8.4. The statement retains the normalizer, inversion, conjugacy, and nonsplit-element coverage properties used in Dickson's classification. Original mathematics and formalization remain attributed to the cited sources; arexychen provides declaration extraction and exact-environment validation.
